<Component name="SliderVsSliderW">
  <VStack padding="{responsive('0.75rem', '2rem')}" gap="0">

    <H1>
      Slider vs SliderW
    </H1>

    <Markdown>
      <![CDATA[
Both the built-in **Slider** (hand-written renderer) and **SliderW**
(extension package built with `wrapCompound`) are running against the same engine.

These tests show what **SliderW** can do that **Slider** can't.
The render component accepts props that the hand-written renderer never forwards.
`wrapCompound` forwards everything automatically, so these "just work."
      ]]>
    </Markdown>

    <!-- === inverted: SliderW only === -->
    <Card var.s6Val="" var.sw6Val="">
      <H2>
        inverted — only works with SliderW
      </H2>
      <Markdown>
        The Radix slider accepts an `inverted` prop that reverses direction.
The hand-written **Slider** renderer never forwards it — silently ignored.
**SliderW** forwards all native props automatically.
      </Markdown>
      <HStack wrapContent="{true}">
        <VStack width="{responsive('100%', '50%')}">
          <Text fontWeight="bold">
            Slider (inverted — ignored)
          </Text>
          <Slider
            inverted="{true}"
            minValue="0"
            maxValue="100"
            step="10"
            initialValue="70"
            onDidChange="{(v) => s6Val = v}" />
          <Text>
            Value: {s6Val}
          </Text>
        </VStack>
        <SpaceFiller />
        <VStack width="{responsive('100%', '50%')}">
          <Text fontWeight="bold">
            SliderW (inverted — works)
          </Text>
          <SliderW
            inverted="{true}"
            minValue="0"
            maxValue="100"
            step="10"
            initialValue="70"
            onDidChange="{(v) => sw6Val = v}" />
          <Text>
            Value: {sw6Val}
          </Text>
        </VStack>
      </HStack>
    </Card>

    <!-- === title: native tooltip on hover === -->
    <Card var.s7Val="" var.sw7Val="">
      <H2>
        title — native HTML tooltip (hover to see)
      </H2>
      <Markdown>
        The render component spreads `...rest` onto its outer div, so standard HTML
attributes like `title` pass through. The hand-written renderer
never forwards it. Hover each slider to compare.
      </Markdown>
      <HStack wrapContent="{true}">
        <VStack width="{responsive('100%', '50%')}">
          <Text fontWeight="bold">
            Slider (title — ignored)
          </Text>
          <Slider
            title="Pick a temperature"
            minValue="0"
            maxValue="100"
            initialValue="50"
            onDidChange="{(v) => s7Val = v}" />
          <Text>
            Value: {s7Val}
          </Text>
        </VStack>
        <SpaceFiller />
        <VStack width="{responsive('100%', '50%')}">
          <Text fontWeight="bold">
            SliderW (title — hover me!)
          </Text>
          <SliderW
            title="Pick a temperature"
            minValue="0"
            maxValue="100"
            initialValue="50"
            onDidChange="{(v) => sw7Val = v}" />
          <Text>
            Value: {sw7Val}
          </Text>
        </VStack>
      </HStack>
    </Card>

    <!-- === aria-label: accessible name and test automation === -->
    <Card>
      <H2>
        aria-label — accessible names for automation
      </H2>
      <Markdown>
        <![CDATA[
Both sliders below set `aria-label="Volume"`. Inspect the DOM to see
which one actually has the attribute on the rendered element.
Playwright can locate the wrapped version with `getByRole('slider', { name: 'Volume' })`.
        ]]>
      </Markdown>
      <HStack wrapContent="{true}">
        <VStack width="{responsive('100%', '50%')}">
          <Text fontWeight="bold">
            Slider (aria-label — ignored)
          </Text>
          <Slider
            aria-label="Volume"
            minValue="0"
            maxValue="100"
            initialValue="50" />
        </VStack>
        <SpaceFiller />
        <VStack width="{responsive('100%', '50%')}">
          <Text fontWeight="bold">
            SliderW (aria-label — works)
          </Text>
          <SliderW
            aria-label="Volume"
            minValue="0"
            maxValue="100"
            initialValue="50" />
        </VStack>
      </HStack>
    </Card>

  </VStack>
</Component>
